WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.975
Unit 2 is administrative remote desktop.

2
00:00:02.975 --> 00:00:09.563
Administrative R D P, S S H and S M B
are the paths an attacker wants most.

3
00:00:09.563 --> 00:00:14.233
Private Access makes each a per-app
application with its own assignment and its own

4
00:00:14.233 --> 00:00:17.549
Conditional Access, so an
administrator authenticates to

5
00:00:17.549 --> 00:00:21.137
Entra with a phishing-resistant
method before the tunnel opens.

6
00:00:21.137 --> 00:00:26.183
Publish administrative hosts as their own
applications, separate from user apps:

7
00:00:26.183 --> 00:00:30.783
one app per tier or host group, with the
host on port thirty-three eighty-nine,

8
00:00:30.783 --> 00:00:35.087
assigned only to the privileged
group whose pim activation grants it.

9
00:00:35.087 --> 00:00:40.376
The policy requires the built-in
phishing-resistant authentication strength,

10
00:00:40.376 --> 00:00:44.624
whose I D ends in four, and a
compliant device, in report-only first.

11
00:00:44.624 --> 00:00:50.312
Enforcement ends the old path: the policy
goes on, and then direct R D P is removed

12
00:00:50.312 --> 00:00:55.540
from the V P N and from the server
firewall, except from the connector I P's.
